.TH webhttrack 1 "@DATE@" "httrack website copier"
.SH NAME
webhttrack \- offline browser : copy websites to a local directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
@SYNOPSIS@
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B webhttrack
starts the
.BR htsserver (1)
web server and opens the WebHTTrack interface in a browser. The interface drives the
.BR httrack (1)
engine to copy websites to a local directory, by default
.IR ~/websites .
The server stops once the interface is closed.
.SH OPTIONS
@OPTIONS@
.SH EXAMPLES
@EXAMPLES@
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP BROWSER
The browser to open, through xdg\-open or sensible\-browser. Without it,
.B webhttrack
tries a list of known browsers.
.IP "LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES, LANG"
The first one set picks the language of the interface, until the interface saves its own choice in
.IR ~/.httrack.ini .
.IP HOME
Projects are kept in
.I ~/websites
unless the interface has saved another folder.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.httrack.ini
.RS
The interface settings. Its
.I path=
line names the projects directory that
.I browse
opens.
.RE
.I ~/.httrack.css
.RS
A stylesheet the interface loads after its own, to change its look.
Without it, the interface reads
.I .httrack.css
in the projects directory, then
.I httrack.css
next to the system
.IR httrack.conf .
.RE
.I ~/.httrack-ui.ini
.RS
The theme chosen on the welcome page.
.RE
.I html/server/themes/
.RS
This folder sits in the httrack data directory, for example
.IR /usr/share/httrack .
Each folder in it that holds a
.I theme.css
is a theme the welcome page offers. A theme loads before
.IR ~/.httrack.css .
.RE
.I ~/.httrack/themes/
.RS
Themes for this user only, laid out the same way. A theme here replaces the
installed theme of the same name, all its files included.
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Each mirror writes its errors and warnings to
.I hts\-log.txt
in the project directory.
@FOOTER@
.PP
The server is
.BR htsserver (1),
and the command-line engine is
.BR httrack (1).
